<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Arcana Model ~ thirteen rooms, one closed set

''The Powers Arcana:'' thirteen rooms partitioning everything a will can do with magic, cut so
the set closes against design history. Operator-approved 2026-08-14 (amendments enacted in the
conversion doctrine); this meme seats the model in the graph so the conversion program, the
FTLS Ch06 restructure, and the composition bag all cite one address.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-thirteen>>

!! The Thirteen

''Three procedural arcana'' — the axes on which magic //systems// differ:
* ''ECM ~ Etheric Counter-Magitech'' — the interference law; ten mode-verbs (scan · veil · jam ·
  spoof · negate · suppress · redirect · capture · absorb · hijack); doctrine, no rows.
* ''Ritual Mechanics'' — the time-for-power trade, cross-arcana.
* ''Ascension'' — how a will climbs: acquisition, initiation, rank (`[skilled]/[expert]/[master]`),
  unlock rites, PP economy, the Immortal ceiling. Re-chartered from Immortal Metaphysics; seats
  the rank-tag rule the FTLS chapters circularly deferred. ''Charter extension (ruled
  2026-08-15):'' the room aligns ''the whole Mortal→Immortal arc'' — BECMI's and every kin
  system's pattern integrities — directly into the noosphere metaphysics-as-gamerules; the
  Pantheon of Arcana stands as its far graduates, reached by climb or by self-assembly, the
  room's ceiling opening onto their floor.

''Ten power arcana'' — the verbs of will (three carry a form fused in, and the fusions mark the
cosmology's scars — life, death's border, the edge):
* ''Mana, Counterspells, and Jamming'' — fuel and its weather
* ''Battle, Elements, and Force'' — //strike//
* ''Biomancy'' — //shape life//
* ''Illusion and Glamour'' — //deceive//
* ''Summoning and Binding'' — //bind another//
* ''Rites of the Deathless'' — //unmake death's border//
* ''Psychic Warfare'' — //compel mind//
* ''Knowledge and Oracle'' — //know//
* ''Alchemy and Artifice'' — //make//
* ''Light and Void'' — //cross the edge//. Charter: the room governs ''the edge of perceived
  reality'' — spectrum, shadow, boundary, transit, temporal exception; Time, gates, and
  reality-rewrites enter as sub-modules of the edge, never as a fourteenth room.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/guard-law>>

!! The Arcana Guard-Law

The thirteen close as a set: the power arcana name ''verbs of will''; the procedural arcana name
''axes of system''. New content enters as a sub-module, a tag, a witness lane, or a procedural
parameter — ''never as a new arcanum''. A fourteenth requires a demonstrated new verb of will,
and the burden of proof sits on the claimant. ''Routing files a power; it does not essentialize
it'': a power lives in one room for provenance and doctrine, and speaks as many rooms'
tag-vocabularies as its fiction earns. New corpora — Ars Magica, the Mage editions, their kin —
enter as ''witness lanes'' feeding the same thirteen.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/blend-law>>

!! The Blend Law (the Mage-1e warning, kept)

First-edition Mage blended sphere-effects and cross-Tradition rotes as the ''normal'' case; later
editions filed effects under single spheres and the conjunctional culture thinned — a design
regression this model refuses to repeat. ''Blends stay first-class:'' the room holds provenance,
the tag-set crosses arcana freely, and the composition bag's `#composes` edge carries true
conjunction at the pattern layer. Same effect under two traditions = one canonical card with
variant callouts (the recognizer law: //Magic Missile → see Tragic Missile//), never a split
essence.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/walk-order>>

!! The Walk of the Thirteen ~ five legs

Proposed order (gated on the braid settling to high confidence; each threshold = operator
sign-off): ''✶ Foundations'' — ECM · Ritual Mechanics · Mana → ''⏿ the Adventurer's Kit'' —
Knowledge · Battle (Shield Ward P:2 seated) · Biomancy → ''◇ the Veiled Rooms'' — Light-and-Void
· Illusion · Psychic → ''▶ the Binding Rooms'' — Summoning · Deathless · Artifice (ends facing
the gear door) → ''↺ Aftermath'' — Ascension's re-seat marks Ch06 alpha.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/word-senses>>

!! Word-Sense Laws ~ one name never blurs

''"Module" splits by owner (ruled):''
* //room-Module// (the doctrine's thirteen) → maps to ''domain-space'' in the composition bag —
  `components/domain/*` plus routing law — never to `modules/*`.
* //card-module// (the bag's `modules/**`) → one power as one pattern-meme with seats and
  components. The name stays here.

''"Arcana" points three ways — and rightly points to all''
//(operator-ruled 2026-08-15)://
# ''The Powers Arcana'' — this meme's thirteen rooms. Owner: the SDM magic grammar.
# ''The Arcana Level'' — the ''Tech/Arcana Level of Areas'': twin 0–20 ratings every Area
  Profile carries — ''Arcane'' (local noosphere weirdness/activity, six banded tiers up to
  event-state) and ''Tech'' (what stands operational + reproducible + teachable). The rating
  powers contest; the Lares Lagrange Nodes place at Tech 16–19. Owner: regions and zones; canon
  verified in the FTLS RSS chapter (Ch04 — Area Profile, Arcane and Tech band tables).
# ''The Pantheon of Arcana'' — ''the Gods: pet-names self-assembled immortal nameless entities
  give themselves'' — each a ''#has-capability-stack spanning all Tech/Arcana Levels''. Owner:
  the entities themselves. ''Modeling law (ruled, deferred until the Powers settle):'' like
  humans, a god can never be modeled in full — but a ''PersonaGroup collection can describe the
  unsayable shape'': the graph holds the group that gestures at the entity, never the entity.
  (Moore's law stands behind it: giant symbolic beings that exist to symbolize and signify —
  and humans need pet-names for nameless pattern-integrities-of-capability.)

The three relate without fusing: the rooms name ''what a will can do'' · the levels name ''how
much a place can carry'' · the Pantheon names ''beings who ride as complete stacks'' — capability
verb × capability saturation × capability totality. One word, three owners, no blur.

